From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nova-cell: do not invent a compute_id

Stop the compute_id delivery from destroying the node identity of a
compute that is already registered, which leaves nova-compute unable to
start -- on every affected host at once, since the cause is a name
comparison that misses the same way everywhere.

The delivery, added for bug 2051011, falls back to
`hypervisor_nodename | to_uuid` whenever the hypervisor lookup returns
nothing. That value is a UUIDv5 of the node name and bears no relation to
the compute_nodes.uuid an already-registered host owns, so delivering it
to a host that is not new makes nova-compute refuse to start:

    nova.exception.DuplicateRecord: Unable to create duplicate record for
    compute node <host>:<generated uuid>
    nova.exception.InvalidConfiguration: Duplicate compute node record
    found for host <host> node <host>

The lookup matches hypervisor names against ansible_facts.nodename, and
the two sides are not computed the same way. nodename is platform.node(),
the raw short hostname. The libvirt driver reports
virConnectGetHostname(), which canonicalises a short, non-localhost name
through getaddrinfo(AI_CANONNAME) and returns the FQDN wherever one
resolves. On a deployment whose hosts resolve to an FQDN the match fails
for every compute at once, and every compute is then handed an identity
that is not its own.

The fallback is not needed. A compute that has never registered takes its
identity from nova, which generates and persists one on first start (see
nova/virt/node.py, get_local_node_uuid). The only reason to write
anything was that nova-compute.json copies compute_id unconditionally and
set_configs fails on a missing source; making that entry conditional
removes the need.

So: drop the generated UUID; remove a stale compute_id when nothing
matched, so one written by an earlier run is not re-delivered; and report
the case where a cloud has hypervisors but none for this host, which is
either a genuinely new compute or the name divergence described above.
---
diff --git a/ansible/roles/nova-cell/tasks/config.yml b/ansible/roles/nova-cell/tasks/config.yml
index 2abcf1822..3bf29f775 100644
--- a/ansible/roles/nova-cell/tasks/config.yml
+++ b/ansible/roles/nova-cell/tasks/config.yml
@@ -100,15 +100,42 @@
         - hypervisors.resources | length > 0
         - matched_hypervisors | length == 1
 
-    # If the host was never registered, create a new hypervisor id and copy as compute_id
-    - name: Generate a new UUID then copy to compute_id
-      ansible.builtin.copy:
-        content: "{{ hypervisor_nodename | to_uuid }}"
-        dest: "{{ node_config_directory }}/nova-compute/compute_id"
-        mode: "0660"
+    # No hypervisor matched this host. Deliver nothing: nova generates and
+    # persists its own node identity on first start, so a host that has never
+    # registered needs no compute_id from here. Inventing one is not safe -- a
+    # UUID derived from the node name bears no relation to the compute_nodes.uuid
+    # an already-registered host owns, and delivering it makes nova-compute
+    # refuse to start with "Duplicate compute node record found".
+    - name: Drop a stale compute_id when no hypervisor matched
+      ansible.builtin.file:
+        path: "{{ node_config_directory }}/nova-compute/compute_id"
+        state: absent
       become: true
       when: hypervisors.resources | length == 0 or matched_hypervisors | length == 0
 
+    # A cloud that already has hypervisors but none for this host is the case
+    # worth naming: either the compute is genuinely new, or its
+    # hypervisor_hostname differs from ansible_facts.nodename -- commonly an FQDN
+    # from DNS against the short kernel name, which diverge because libvirt
+    # canonicalises the hostname and Ansible does not.
+    - name: Report that no hypervisor matched this host
+      ansible.builtin.debug:
+        msg: >-
+          No hypervisor is named '{{ hypervisor_nodename }}', but this cloud has
+          {{ hypervisors.resources | length }}. If this compute is not new, its
+          hypervisor_hostname differs from ansible_facts.nodename and no
+          compute_id can be derived; nova-compute keeps the identity it already
+          holds.
+      when:
+        - hypervisors.resources | length > 0
+        - matched_hypervisors | default([]) | length == 0
+
+    - name: Record whether a compute_id is delivered for this host
+      ansible.builtin.set_fact:
+        nova_compute_id_delivered: >-
+          {{ hypervisors.resources | length > 0
+             and matched_hypervisors | default([]) | length == 1 }}
+
 - name: Copying over config.json files for services
   become: true
   template:
diff --git a/ansible/roles/nova-cell/templates/nova-compute.json.j2 b/ansible/roles/nova-cell/templates/nova-compute.json.j2
index cba0462af..8d11be7bd 100644
--- a/ansible/roles/nova-cell/templates/nova-compute.json.j2
+++ b/ansible/roles/nova-cell/templates/nova-compute.json.j2
@@ -6,13 +6,13 @@
             "dest": "/etc/nova/nova.conf",
             "owner": "nova",
             "perm": "0600"
-        },
+        }{% if nova_compute_id_delivered | default(false) | bool %},
         {
             "source": "{{ container_config_directory }}/compute_id",
             "dest": "/var/lib/nova/compute_id",
             "owner": "nova",
             "perm": "0600"
-        }{% if nova_policy_file is defined %},
+        }{% endif %}{% if nova_policy_file is defined %},
         {
             "source": "{{ container_config_directory }}/{{ nova_policy_file }}",
             "dest": "/etc/nova/{{ nova_policy_file }}",
